course: dictionary
lesson: 3220
title: Words about power and freedom
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Enslave is a strong word. It comes from slave, and it means to make people into slaves: to own them and force them to work without pay or freedom. «Enslaved people worked on plantations without pay or freedom» tells you what that looks like.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Without pay and without freedom show that people had no choice about their work. Families could be sold apart, so enslave is not a small or light word. It describes people being treated as property.
explain: Enslave can also be used in a figurative way, for a habit or a feeling that controls you so completely that you cannot stop. Check the meaning by swapping in «control completely» and seeing if the sentence still makes sense. Figurative means the word is used to make a comparison, not to talk about real people.
fact: Enslave is a verb: enslave, enslaves, enslaved, enslaving.
fact: «Enslaved» means made into a slave, owned by others and forced to work.
fact: «Sugar cane plantations in Brazil and the Caribbean were worked mainly by enslaved Africans.»
fact: Even when people were enslaved, they kept music, faith, stories and families alive. Their spirit was not owned.
fact: Slavery is deeply wrong, and historians study it so that people remember and learn from what happened.
exercise: «Enslaved people worked on plantations without pay or freedom.» What does enslaved mean here? | Free to choose their own job | Given a big reward for hard work | Living in a busy city | *Made into slaves, owned and forced to work
exercise: «Ben's phone habit had enslaved him: he could not put it down, even at dinner.» What does enslaved mean here? | *Controlled him so completely that he could not stop | Bought him a new phone | Made him very happy | Set free from the habit
exercise: «Enslaved people worked on plantations without pay or freedom.» Which word shows they got no wages? | *pay | plantations | stories | music
test: «Enslaved people kept music, faith and stories alive.» What does this show? | They forgot their music and stories | They were allowed to leave whenever they wanted | *Their culture stayed strong even though they were not free | They were paid well for their work
test: Which word means the opposite of enslave? | control | owned | *free | forced
exam: What is the best meaning of enslave? | To run very fast | To tell someone a long story | To give someone a gift | *To make people slaves, owned and forced to work without pay or freedom
